     "text": "{\"count\":4,\"rationale\":\"A 4-step block works: block the target's four parents (dbReplica:collection, codeRepo:collection, shareMount:collection, vaultRead:collection). Fewer than 4 is impossible. (1) dbReplica needs domainAdmin cut, via dbReplica, domainAdmin, backupHost or ssoLogin. shareMount also needs jumpHost cut, and jumpHost is fed by browserStore (fed by the supplychain foothold) and memoryDump (fed by the phishing foothold). No single block stops both shareMount and dbReplica, so they need 2 blocks. Every 2-block pair that does stop both (shareMount or jumpHost, plus one of dbReplica, domainAdmin, backupHost or ssoLogin) leaves vaultRead reachable via fileServer:lateralMovement, which is fed by memoryDump (phishing foothold). It also leaves codeRepo reachable via monitoringHost:lateralMovement, which is fed by tokenCache (supplychain foothold). (2) No single further block stops both vaultRead and codeRepo, since fileServer and monitoringHost need separate blocks. So at least 2 + 2 = 4.\"}"
    }
